From d5f76457594a5f877050fcf737b36531f22e91ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:58:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] NodalBlockJacobi: empty processes, block sizes, exact checks

From the independent review of the preconditioner:
- a process owning no unknown no longer fails (nothing is factorized or
  applied);
- the size of the blocks is one or the number of components of the
  unknowns, other sizes giving blocks which are not nodal being refused,
  and the size of the operator is checked before its nodal blocks are
  computed;
- the decoding of the layouts of the unknowns is shared by the kernels;
- the documentation tells that the damping factor does not change the
  iterates of the Krylov solvers, that a singular block stops the
  computation in MFEM, that only MAGMA computes on its own queue, that the
  blocks of the operator applied without assembly are approximated on a
  non conforming mesh, and that the LU factors are slightly more accurate
  in single precision.

NodalBlockJacobiTest compares the application of the preconditioner with
the inverses of the nodal blocks computed on the host (from the matrix,
or from its diagonal block in parallel), for each backend, factorization
and with a damping factor, and checks the refusal of a block size of two.
The cantilever beam of the test moves to tests/ElasticitySystem.hxx.
